    given-names: Hsiu-Chi
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7421-8027"
    alias: thc1006
repository-code: "https://github.com/thc1006/qwen3.8-speculative-decoding-rtx3090"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC0-1.0
keywords:
  - speculative decoding
  - llama.cpp
  - inference benchmarking
  - reproducibility
  - preregistration
  - RTX 3090
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22149941
version: 1.0.1
date-released: "2026-08-28"
# The DOI above is the CONCEPT one, which resolves to whichever version is newest; the v1.0.0
# deposit itself is 10.5281/zenodo.22149942, and v1.0.1 gets its own on deposit. v1.0.0 stays
# where it is: a deposit is a record of what was published, not a draft, and the corrections are
# in PREREGISTRATION.md where anyone reading either version can find them. It could not be written before the release existed,
# because Zenodo mints it from the release -- so the archived v1.0.0 tree does not name its own
# DOI and no tagged tree ever can. `date-released` is 08-28 and not 08-29 because that is what
# Zenodo published and what the release's created_at says in UTC; the tag was made at 03:18 on
# 08-29 in +0800, which is the same instant. Two citable records of one release disagreeing by a
# day is the kind of small false note this repository exists to not make.
